      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For your MSA, you absolutely need a robust clause covering price adjustments, which should be tied to clear, objective metrics, not just the supplier's whim. You must also include a Force Majeure clause that specifically addresses supply chain disruptions, detailing notification procedures and remedies. Furthermore, strong warranties regarding material quality and compliance are crucial to ensure the raw materials meet your Munich plant's exacting standards. Finally, define clear termination rights for both parties, especially if performance falls below agreed-upon thresholds.",
