    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. Regarding the price adjustments, how do we make sure they don't try to sneak in extra fees or \"hidden costs\" midway through a contract? I want to make sure we aren't getting blindsided by things that aren't explicitly in the main price list.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To prevent sneaky fees, you need a very detailed \"Scope of Supply\" or \"Pricing Schedule\" appendix that is explicitly incorporated into the MSA. This document should itemize *everything*—shipping costs, tariffs, packaging fees, quality inspection charges, everything—so there are no gray areas for them to exploit. You should also mandate that any *change* to this schedule requires a formal, written Change Order signed by both parties, detailing the exact cost impact. This locks down the terms, preventing them from adding extra charges later on.",
      "source": "target",
