    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That sounds solid. One more thing—how should we phrase the section on \"bad faith\" or dishonest behavior from their side? We've had issues in the past where vendors act one way during negotiations but then try to undermine the partnership once the contract is signed. I want the contract to have some teeth to deal with those kinds of bad actors.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can address this by incorporating a \"Cooperation and Good Faith\" clause, which requires the supplier to act honestly and in a manner consistent with the mutual goals of the agreement. This is where you can put in the teeth, as you'd want to tie breaches of this clause to material breach provisions. If they act in bad faith, it should allow you to seek remedies, potentially including termination for cause, much like a standard contract violation. It's a powerful clause, but make sure the definition of \"bad faith\" is reasonably tied to demonstrable actions, not just suspicion.",
      "source": "target",
